Sara and I walk out of the sports hall.
It is late, and it is a cold winter evening.
But I am still warm after the match.
We walk over to the bus stop together.
The wind is blowing, and the street is dark.
"Do you also like to play badminton at the weekend?" I ask.
"No, I only play badminton on Thursdays," Sara answers.
"But I like to do sports," she says.
"I usually go for a run in the park," she continues.
She is a very active and fun person.
We wait for the bus in the cold.
"My bus comes in ten minutes," I say.
"We take the same bus," Sara smiles.
I am very happy about that.
I like to talk with her.
Kasper and Sara are fun and nice people.
Now I have a good routine on Thursdays.
I am tired, but I am in a good mood.
The bus finally arrives.
I am already looking forward to next Thursday.
